  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "passage.school-garden",
      "title": "The School Garden",
      "level": "A2",
      "source": "original",
      "interests": [
        "school",
        "science"
      ],
      "text": "Last year, the students in Maya's class started a garden behind their school. At first, nobody believed it would work. The ground was dry, and there was very little shade. The students did not give up. They collected rainwater in old buckets and planted herbs that do not need much water. Every morning before class, two students checked the plants. By the spring, the garden was full of mint, basil and small tomatoes. Now the school cafeteria uses the herbs in its salads, and younger students visit the garden to learn about plants. Maya says the best part was not the vegetables. \"We learned that a small group can change a place,\" she said."
    }
